<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Abraham on John, Complected</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/abraham/</link><description>Recent content in Abraham on John, Complected</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2026</copyright><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/abraham/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Remember Who You Are — I Have Called You by Name</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-i-have-called-you-by-name/</link><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-i-have-called-you-by-name/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis&amp;#43;12%3A1%E2%80%934&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Genesis 12:1–4&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt; and &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis&amp;#43;17%3A1%E2%80%937&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Genesis 17:1–7&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;139%3A1%E2%80%9318&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 139:1–18&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There can be something unsettling about feeling less certain of yourself than you once did. Names can become harder to remember. Familiar things can sometimes feel unfamiliar. Even our own story can become more difficult to hold together.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But God does not know us in the uncertain way that we sometimes know ourselves. &lt;strong&gt;He knows us completely.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>